// Official skill -> caster action mapping for the client.
//
// Generated by `tools/gen_skill_actions.py`; do not edit by hand.
// Regenerate with: `./tools/gen_skill_actions.py`
// Drift check:      `./tools/gen_skill_actions.py --check`
//
// Facts extracted from the official client's skill action assignment
// (`tools/data/windows_client_skill_actions.json`, roBrowserLegacy RE dump of the
// Windows client tables). Only numeric ids and action names are extracted.
//
// Rows corrected by the curated `overrides` section of
// `tools/data/skill_actions_extra.json`: the official client's
// `CSession::GetSkillActionInfo` motion is an ACTORSTATEID, and
// `CGameActor::SetState` maps it to the ACT action index recorded there.
//
// Format: (skill id, action). Actions: Attack, Idle, Pickup, Skill,
// ReadyFight, Stand (see `CasterAction` in `ro-next/src/world/skill_action.rs`).
// Skills that are not listed use `Skill`, the client's default casting
// gesture.
//
// Rows may also carry `use_action`, the pose of the `ZC_USE_SKILL`
// (0x09CB) path, which the official client drives with
// `CSession::GetSkillActionInfo2` (default `motion = 7`). The main
// `action` stays the `ZC_USESKILL_ACK` (0x0B1A) pose from
// `GetSkillActionInfo` (default `motion = 8`); `use_action` is emitted
// only where the two disagree. `Keep` means `SetState(-1)` (no pose
// change).
//
// Rows may also carry the official frame sequence (`SetFrameSequence`):
// (first, last, loop_to, duration_ms, interval_ticks). `interval_ticks` is
// the preceding `SetSequenceInterval(N)` in 60 Hz update ticks (Fury: 30 =
// 500 ms per frame); 0 keeps the ACT frame delay.
//
// `cast_sequence` is the official cast-start pose hold
// (`CGameMode::ApplyActorSkillState`): (first, last, loop_to,
// after_cast_ms, interval_ticks). It is applied when `ZC_USESKILL_ACK`
// starts a cast and lasts the packet cast time + `after_cast_ms`
// (MO_STEELBODY: `duration + 1000`). The Brandish Spear / Bowling Bash
// motion freeze is modelled as the same frame-0 hold of the attack block.
//
// `Stand` is the official `ST_STAND` (`motion = 0`): block 0 for every
// non-local actor, block 32 for the local player (`CPc`). `Idle` stays
// the client's armed idle pose for the curated "prevent default" rows.
//
// The file is loaded at runtime through the normal client file loader, so a
// server can override it without rebuilding the client; the compiled Rust
// table is only the fallback for missing files.
(
    provenance: "roBrowserLegacy (GPL-3.0) RE dump of the official client tables; only numeric ids, action names and hold flags are extracted",
